<!--
    RE-friction round 2, need `argument-recovery-knobs-still` (challenge
    6547b4d50f4238b24302b588, PE x86-64 `trappy attack.exe`): `kuna decompile
    ... 0x1400011c0 -addr` renders the same allocator with two arities, nine
    lines apart, and `option calleearity on` does NOT fix it:

        v10 = (char ****)sub_140002c90(v11 + 0x27);   0x1400016d1
        v19 = (char *****)sub_140002c90();            0x1400016f7

    Root cause (P4, trial finalization).  This is MSVC's aligned operator new,
    whose two arms call the same allocator:

        cmp  rcx,0x1000
        jc   small                ; rcx = the requested size
        lea  rax,[rcx+0x27]
        cmp  rax,rcx
        jbe  abort                ; the overflow guard
        mov  rcx,rax
        call operator_new         ; LARGE: rcx written here, recovered
      small:
        test rcx,rcx
        jz   nothing
        call operator_new         ; SMALL: rcx live-in, dropped

    The small arm never rewrites rcx, so the Varnode reaching the CALL is the
    one the `test` branches on and Funcdata::onlyOpUse (funcdata_varnode.cc:1851)
    rejects the trial.  `calleearity` exists for exactly this and still declines,
    because ActionActiveParam finalizes each call spec the moment it is fully
    checked, in qlst order: measured on the witness, the SMALL site 0x1400016f7
    finalizes with an empty witness list while its sibling 0x1400016d1, which
    recovers exactly RCX, is still input_active.  A site is only reconciled
    against the sites BEFORE it, and here the loser is first.

    Reordering the finalization is the wrong fix: Funcdata::checkCallDoubleUse
    (funcdata_varnode.cc:2121) reads whether ANOTHER spec is still input-active
    while scoring a trial, so deferring a spec past its neighbours'
    checkInputTrialUse changes argument recovery on every binary.  Instead the
    call that finalizes with an EMPTY argument list is set aside, with the
    Varnodes its promotable trials point at, and retried once at the end of the
    same pass when every spec is final.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "trial-finalization".  The P0 assertion
    `option calleearityfwd on|off` decides whether that retry happens; it reuses
    every one of `calleearity`'s refusals and is inert with `calleearity off`.

    The fixture is the same construct on SysV x86-64 (rdi rather than rcx),
    assembled from:

        callee: mov %rdi,%rax ; add $1,%rax ; ret
        caller: sub $0x28,%rsp
                cmp $0x1000,%rdi
                jb  small
                lea 0x27(%rdi),%rax
                cmp %rdi,%rax
                jbe bail
                mov %rax,%rdi
                call callee        # LARGE: fresh rdi, keeps its argument
                add $0x28,%rsp ; ret
        small:  test %rdi,%rdi
                jz  zero
                call callee        # SMALL: rdi live-in, and the guard reads it
                add $0x28,%rsp ; ret
        zero:   xor %eax,%eax ; add $0x28,%rsp ; ret
        bail:   xor %eax,%eax ; add $0x28,%rsp ; ret

    The SMALL site is laid out after the LARGE one and reached by a forward
    branch, which is what puts it FIRST in qlst order and so out of
    `calleearity`'s reach, the whole point of this testcase.

    Pass 1 (`option calleearityfwd off`) reproduces the BUG: the small arm
    renders as `callee()` while the large arm keeps `callee(a0 + 0x27)`.
    Pass 2 (`option calleearityfwd on`) is the FIX: the small arm passes `a0`,
    the size the disassembly actually leaves in rdi, and the large arm is
    untouched, no argument is fabricated at the site that was already right.
-->
